# drive.defaults — GLOBAL defaults for drive.sh, shared by every feature/run.
# One-time install:
#   mkdir -p ~/.config/pipeline-driver && cp drive.defaults.example ~/.config/pipeline-driver/drive.defaults
# Sourced by bash BEFORE the per-feature drive.config, so anything here is a
# default and drive.config always wins. Keep per-feature facts (WORKDIR, BRANCH,
# FEATURE, the per-run HERDR_PANE_ID) OUT of this file.
#
# Slot bindings on this machine — machine-readable: `coordinate.sh doctor|status`
# print these, and doctor verifies each *_MODEL_EXPECT against the live pane
# footer (fail-closed when set). coordinate.config may override any of them
# (config wins). prd/arch/task run in the CC pane; impl in the PI_WORKDIR pane;
# review in the CODEX_WORKDIR pane. *_MODEL_EXPECT is a literal case-insensitive
# ASCII substring of the pane footer/title (charset is printable ASCII — control
# bytes and bytes ≥0x80 are rejected); unset = skip that check.
CC_AGENT=claude
# CC_MODEL_EXPECT=
IMPL_AGENT=pi                 # pi | kimi | ... — the TUI driven in the impl pane
IMPL_MODEL_EXPECT=glm-5.2     # e.g. kimi-k3 when IMPL_AGENT=kimi
REVIEW_AGENT=codex
REVIEW_MODEL_EXPECT=gpt-5.6

# --- impl transport + model (stable across features) ---------------------------
# claude: spawn a headless `claude` child per card. herdr: type IMPL_SLASH_CMD into a
# live coder TUI in a Herdr pane and poll the remote journal (use when the impl
# model's plan only allows interactive coding tools) — `herdr pane run`, read-first
# {done,idle} guard, fails closed unless Herdr's agent detection is
# hook/manifest-authoritative.
IMPL_TRANSPORT=herdr
IMPL_SLASH_CMD=/skill:pipeline-impl   # pi registers skills as /skill:<name>
# HERDR_RESET_CMD=/new                # herdr: per-card TUI reset (both sides guarded); empty = off
# HERDR_PANE_CWD_MATCH=               # herdr: cwd SUBSTRING replacing the ==WORKDIR pane filter (TUI in a subdir)
# TUI_SKILLS_DIR=$HOME/.pi/agent/skills   # where the TUI agent loads skills; doctor checks the impl slot resolves THERE
# IMPL_MODEL=haiku                    # claude transport only; floor haiku, any alias or model id
# Gateway (claude transport, non-Anthropic Anthropic-compatible model, e.g. GLM):
# IMPL_AUTH_TOKEN_ENV names an EXISTING env var holding the token (never written here).
# IMPL_BASE_URL=
# IMPL_AUTH_TOKEN_ENV=

# --- loop tuning ----------------------------------------------------------------
# CARD_TIMEOUT=2700          # herdr transport: max seconds to wait for one card
# POLL_SECS=30               # herdr transport: journal poll interval
# HERDR_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS=60000 # herdr: status-guard budget before each send
# HERDR_RESET_SETTLE_MS=2000  # herdr: post-reset window to observe the TUI taking the reset
# MAX_CONSEC_FAIL=2          # circuit breaker: consecutive failed impl runs
# RETRY_ON_FAIL=1            # 1 = auto-retry informed failures (attempts<3); 0 = halt each
# SETTINGS=/abs/path/to/settings.driver.json   # claude transport --settings template

# --- YOLO: standing ex-ante grant (README §YOLO) --------------------------------
# 1 = record ONCE that, for LOW-RISK features driven on this machine, the
# coordinating agent may read the frozen spec and echo the spec-rev at GATE 1 —
# no per-run chat authorization needed. This does NOT auto-start drive (starting
# ./drive.sh stays an explicit per-feature act), never delegates the merge
# confirm, and DANGEROUS features (external write-paths) never use the driver.
YOLO=0

# --- sibling repos (drive.sh doctor, board rendering) ------------------------------
# PIPELINE_REPO=$HOME/workspace/pipeline
# DASHBOARD_REPO=$HOME/workspace/pipeline-dashboard
# SKILLS_DIR=$HOME/.agents/skills

# --- board auto-refresh -------------------------------------------------------------
# Non-empty = re-render the read-only dashboard here after GATE 1, after every
# advanced card, and on halt (needs node + a built DASHBOARD_REPO). Open it in a
# browser and refresh whenever you glance over.
# BOARD_OUT=/tmp/pipeline-board.html

# --- walk-away notify hook (README §Board & walk-away notify) ------------------------
# Non-empty = invoke this ABSOLUTE-path executable (best-effort) at the same three
# moments as BOARD_OUT — after GATE 1, after every advanced card, and on every halt.
# Event in $1 (gate1|card|halt); context in DRIVE_* env (DRIVE_EVENT / DRIVE_FEATURE /
# DRIVE_BRANCH / DRIVE_WORKDIR / DRIVE_TRANSPORT / DRIVE_SEQ / DRIVE_STATUS / DRIVE_NEXT,
# plus DRIVE_HALT_REASON + DRIVE_HALT_NEXT on halts). Validated at preflight — a broken
# notifier halts BEFORE GATE 1 (you are about to walk away trusting these pings);
# runtime send failures warn once and never halt the loop. One-way driver->human.
# Defense-in-depth, NOT a sandbox. NOTIFY_EXEC is a TRUSTED executable that runs as
# YOUR user (normal filesystem/process/network access — it is NOT OS-isolated).
# Three measures limit accidental damage / accidental credential leakage:
#   * NOTIFY_TIMEOUT_MS (default 5000) — a validated positive integer (hard
#     per-invocation deadline; out of range is rejected at preflight). A wedged or
#     TERM-immune send is killed — its WHOLE process group, via perl setpgrp (TERM
#     then KILL; perl is REQUIRED when NOTIFY_EXEC is set) — and degrades to one warn.
#   * the notifier's stdin is /dev/null (immediate EOF) — it cannot consume the
#     GATE 1 / rejection-gate prompt or later operator input.
#   * the notifier launches under `env -i` with an explicit allowlist — it receives
#     ONLY PATH/HOME + the DRIVE_* context + the NAMES in NOTIFY_ENV_ALLOW. Ambient
#     EXPORTED variables (GH_TOKEN / ANTHROPIC_* / the var named by IMPL_AUTH_TOKEN_ENV)
#     are NOT inherited unless allowed. Environment allowlist ONLY — the hook can still
#     read files under HOME or write DRIVE_WORKDIR, so this guards accidental env
#     leakage, not a credential/OS boundary. Deny by default; opt a variable in here:
# NOTIFY_ENV_ALLOW="HERMES_TOKEN TG_CHAT_ID"
# Canonical adapter (Hermes -> Telegram):
# Source (public sibling): git clone https://github.com/jackypanster/pipeline-dispatch.git
# NOTIFY_EXEC=$HOME/workspace/pipeline-dispatch/notify.sh

# The meta-PR review<->fix relay is NOT a driver span. It lives in the
# `pipeline-coordinate` playbook (Profile A): a CC session dispatches the fixer and
# reviewer panes over Herdr and reads verdicts off the PR. The driver's own
# review-drive.sh + one-key relay were retired with the orca transport.
